[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: MIL-STD-498 SRS (Software Requirements Specification) - ADAS Control Module

[SECTION]
TITLE: 1. Scope

[SECTION]
TITLE: 1.1 Identification

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-001
TITLE: Software Identification
STATEMENT: The software shall be identified as the Advanced Driver Assistance System (ADAS) Control Module Software Requirements Specification, version 1.0, for automotive safety-critical applications.
RATIONALE: Proper software identification ensures configuration management and traceability for safety-critical automotive systems.

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 1.2 System overview

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-002
TITLE: System Overview
STATEMENT: The ADAS Control Module software shall provide comprehensive driver assistance capabilities including lane departure warning, adaptive cruise control, forward collision warning, blind spot detection, and traffic sign recognition through real-time sensor fusion and decision-making algorithms.
RATIONALE: System overview establishes the context for all software requirements in the automotive safety domain.

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 1.3 Document overview

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-003
TITLE: Document Structure
STATEMENT: This document shall be organized into six major sections covering scope, referenced documents, requirements, qualification provisions, traceability, and notes, following MIL-STD-498 and ISO 26262 standards.
RATIONALE: Structured organization facilitates requirements review and validation for safety-critical systems.

[/SECTION]

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 2. Referenced documents

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-004
TITLE: Reference Standards
STATEMENT: The software shall comply with MIL-STD-498, ISO 26262 ASIL D, MISRA C++ 2023, AUTOSAR 4.4, and automotive cybersecurity standards (ISO 21434) for software development and quality assurance.
RATIONALE: Compliance with established automotive standards ensures software quality, safety, and security.

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 3. Requirements

[SECTION]
TITLE: 3.1 Required states and modes

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-005
TITLE: Operational States
STATEMENT: The software shall support normal operation, degraded operation, emergency operation, maintenance mode, and shutdown states with appropriate state transitions and safety interlocks.
RATIONALE: Defined operational states ensure predictable system behavior under various automotive conditions.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-006
TITLE: Mode Transitions
STATEMENT: The software shall provide automatic and manual mode transitions with appropriate safety checks, driver notifications, and graceful degradation capabilities.
RATIONALE: Controlled mode transitions prevent system instability and ensure driver safety.

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 3.2 CSCI capability requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-007
TITLE: Lane Departure Warning
STATEMENT: The software shall detect lane departures within 100ms using camera and sensor fusion, providing visual and audible warnings to the driver with configurable sensitivity levels.
RATIONALE: Lane departure warning is a critical safety feature that prevents accidents and saves lives.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-008
TITLE: Adaptive Cruise Control
STATEMENT: The software shall maintain safe following distance using radar and camera sensors, automatically adjusting vehicle speed within 50ms of detecting speed changes in the lead vehicle.
RATIONALE: Adaptive cruise control enhances driver comfort and safety during highway driving.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-009
TITLE: Forward Collision Warning
STATEMENT: The software shall detect potential forward collisions within 200ms and provide escalating warnings (visual, audible, haptic) with automatic emergency braking if driver does not respond.
RATIONALE: Forward collision warning and automatic emergency braking are critical safety features that prevent accidents.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-010
TITLE: Blind Spot Detection
STATEMENT: The software shall monitor blind spots using radar sensors and provide visual warnings in side mirrors and audible alerts when turn signals are activated with vehicles in blind spots.
RATIONALE: Blind spot detection prevents lane change accidents and enhances driver awareness.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-011
TITLE: Traffic Sign Recognition
STATEMENT: The software shall recognize and display traffic signs including speed limits, stop signs, and warning signs using camera-based image processing with 95% accuracy.
RATIONALE: Traffic sign recognition enhances driver awareness and compliance with traffic regulations.

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 3.3 CSCI external interface requirements

[SECTION]
TITLE: 3.3.1 Interface identification and diagrams

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-012
TITLE: Sensor Interface
STATEMENT: The software shall interface with front radar, rear radar, side radar, front camera, rear camera, and ultrasonic sensors through CAN bus and Ethernet protocols with redundancy.
RATIONALE: Sensor interfaces are critical for accurate environmental perception and safety system operation.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-013
TITLE: Vehicle Control Interface
STATEMENT: The software shall interface with engine control unit, brake control unit, steering control unit, and transmission control unit through secure CAN bus communication.
RATIONALE: Vehicle control interfaces enable ADAS functions to influence vehicle behavior for safety.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-014
TITLE: Human Machine Interface
STATEMENT: The software shall provide driver interface through instrument cluster, head-up display, and center console with configurable warning levels and system status information.
RATIONALE: Human machine interface ensures driver awareness and system transparency.

[/SECTION]

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 3.4 CSCI internal interface requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-015
TITLE: Internal Communication
STATEMENT: The software shall use secure internal communication protocols between components with message queuing, event-driven architecture, and fault-tolerant message delivery.
RATIONALE: Internal communication protocols ensure system reliability and maintainability for safety-critical functions.

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 3.5 CSCI internal data requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-016
TITLE: Data Storage
STATEMENT: The software shall store sensor calibration data, system configuration, operational logs, diagnostic information, and safety event records with appropriate data retention and archival policies.
RATIONALE: Data storage requirements ensure system auditability, diagnostic capabilities, and operational continuity.

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 3.6 Adaptation requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-017
TITLE: Configuration Management
STATEMENT: The software shall support dynamic configuration updates for sensor parameters, warning thresholds, and system behavior without system restart, including over-the-air updates.
RATIONALE: Dynamic configuration enables system adaptation to changing vehicle and environmental conditions.

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 3.7 Sizing and timing requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-018
TITLE: Performance Requirements
STATEMENT: The software shall process sensor data within 10ms, respond to critical safety events within 50ms, and maintain system responsiveness under all operating conditions.
RATIONALE: Performance requirements ensure system responsiveness under expected automotive load conditions.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-019
TITLE: Memory Requirements
STATEMENT: The software shall operate within 512MB RAM and 2GB flash memory with efficient memory management and garbage collection for long-term operation.
RATIONALE: Memory requirements ensure system stability and performance in resource-constrained automotive environments.

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 3.8 Safety requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-020
TITLE: Safety Controls
STATEMENT: The software shall implement safety controls to prevent unauthorized vehicle control commands, ensure graceful degradation during failures, and maintain system stability under all conditions.
RATIONALE: Safety requirements protect vehicle occupants and prevent system failures that could cause accidents.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-021
TITLE: Fault Tolerance
STATEMENT: The software shall implement redundant processing paths, sensor fusion algorithms, and fault detection mechanisms to ensure system reliability and safety.
RATIONALE: Fault tolerance ensures system operation even when individual components fail.

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 3.9 Security and privacy requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-022
TITLE: Cybersecurity
STATEMENT: The software shall implement automotive cybersecurity controls including secure boot, encrypted communication, intrusion detection, and secure over-the-air updates.
RATIONALE: Cybersecurity is critical for preventing unauthorized access and ensuring vehicle safety.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-023
TITLE: Data Privacy
STATEMENT: The software shall implement data privacy controls for driver information, location data, and vehicle telemetry with configurable data sharing policies.
RATIONALE: Data privacy controls protect driver information and comply with privacy regulations.

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 3.10 Quality requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-024
TITLE: Reliability
STATEMENT: The software shall achieve 99.999% uptime with mean time between failures exceeding 10,000 hours and comprehensive error handling and recovery mechanisms.
RATIONALE: High reliability is essential for safety-critical automotive systems.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-025
TITLE: Maintainability
STATEMENT: The software shall be designed for maintainability with modular architecture, comprehensive logging, diagnostic capabilities, and remote monitoring support.
RATIONALE: Maintainability ensures long-term system viability and cost-effective operation.

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 4. Qualification provisions

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-026
TITLE: Testing Requirements
STATEMENT: The software shall undergo comprehensive testing including unit tests, integration tests, system tests, safety tests, and field validation tests with 100% requirements coverage.
RATIONALE: Comprehensive testing ensures software quality and safety compliance.

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 5. Requirements traceability

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-027
TITLE: Traceability Matrix
STATEMENT: All software requirements shall be traceable to system requirements, design elements, test cases, and validation activities through a comprehensive traceability matrix.
RATIONALE: Requirements traceability ensures complete requirement coverage and facilitates change impact analysis.

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 6. Notes

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-028
TITLE: Implementation Notes
STATEMENT: The software shall be implemented using MISRA C++ compliant code with static analysis, code reviews, and continuous integration practices for quality assurance.
RATIONALE: Implementation notes provide guidance for development teams and ensure code quality.

[/SECTION] 